#: src/modules/filesystem.md:6
msgid "Filesystem Hierarchy"
msgstr ""

#: src/modules/filesystem.md:8
msgid ""
"Omitting the module content will tell Rust to look for it in another file:"
msgstr ""

#: src/modules/filesystem.md:11 src/modules/filesystem.md:30
#: src/modules/filesystem.md:73
msgid "// Copyright 2022 Google LLC\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/modules/filesystem.md:12 src/modules/filesystem.md:31
#: src/modules/filesystem.md:74
msgid "// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/modules/filesystem.md:17
msgid ""
"This tells Rust that the `garden` module content is found at `src/garden."
"rs`. Similarly, a `garden::vegetables` module can be found at `src/garden/"
"vegetables.rs`."
msgstr ""

#: src/modules/filesystem.md:21
msgid "The `crate` root is in:"
msgstr ""

#: src/modules/filesystem.md:23
msgid "`src/lib.rs` (for a library crate)"
msgstr ""

#: src/modules/filesystem.md:24
msgid "`src/main.rs` (for a binary crate)"
msgstr ""

#: src/modules/filesystem.md:26
msgid ""
"Modules defined in files can be documented, too, using \"inner doc "
"comments\". These document the item that contains them -- in this case, a "
"module."
msgstr ""

#: src/modules/filesystem.md:32
msgid ""
"//! This module implements the garden, including a highly performant "
"germination\n"
"//! implementation.\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/modules/filesystem.md:35
msgid "// Re-export types from this module.\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/modules/filesystem.md:39
msgid "/// Sow the given seed packets.\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/modules/filesystem.md:44
msgid "/// Harvest the produce in the garden that is ready.\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/modules/filesystem.md:54
msgid ""
"Before Rust 2018, modules needed to be located at `module/mod.rs` instead of "
"`module.rs`, and this is still a working alternative for editions after 2018."
msgstr ""

#: src/modules/filesystem.md:57
msgid ""
"The main reason to introduce `filename.rs` as alternative to `filename/mod."
"rs` was because many files named `mod.rs` can be hard to distinguish in IDEs."
msgstr ""

#: src/modules/filesystem.md:60
msgid "Deeper nesting can use folders, even if the main module is a file:"
msgstr ""

#: src/modules/filesystem.md:70
msgid ""
"The place Rust will look for modules can be changed with a compiler "
"directive:"
msgstr ""

#: src/modules/filesystem.md:76
msgid "\"some/path.rs\""
msgstr ""

#: src/modules/filesystem.md:80
msgid ""
"This is useful, for example, if you would like to place tests for a module "
"in a file named `some_module_test.rs`, similar to the convention in Go."
msgstr ""
